# Fallback denylist for legacy (non-BuildKit) builders, which ignore the
# per-Dockerfile `<tool>/docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore` allowlist next to the
# Dockerfile. That file is the primary build-context filter under BuildKit;
# this one exists purely as defense in depth so that a
# `DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0 docker build -f <tool>/docker/Dockerfile .` never ships
# secrets, databases, or repo metadata to the daemon.

# Secrets and runtime data
**/settings.env
**/settings-*.env
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.log
**/data/
**/BUILD_INFO

# Repository metadata, CI, docs, agent notes, and tests (none is needed inside an image)
.git/
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
.github/
docs/
site/
**/tests/
**/grafana/

# Caches, virtual environments, and local tooling state
**/.venv/
**/.venv.*
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.omc/
**/.claude/
